LibreTripoSplat includes code ported from TripoSplat:

Source: https://github.com/VAST-AI-Research/TripoSplat (commit d8db9e018b413dd9c4a9fe22463781bf98e8e68d)
License: MIT.
Copyright (c) 2026 VAST. Authors: Runjie Yan, Yan-Pei Cao, Peng Wang,
Ding Liang, Yuan-Chen Guo (TripoAI).

The port covers inference: the denoiser (LatentSeqMMFlowModel), the octree
and Gaussian decoders (OctreeGaussianDecoder), the upstream configuration
constants, the flow sampler with its guidance convention, and the Gaussian
activation. Parameter names mirror upstream so the released safetensors
load with strict=True. Changes from upstream: the octree sampler and the
leaf jitter draw from an explicit torch.Generator (upstream draws from the
global generator, so its decoder stage is not seed-reproducible); the
quaternions are normalised (upstream writes the raw biased quaternion to
the PLY, which viewers normalise); TensorDict-free plain tensors; the
networks run in fp16 on CUDA and MPS as upstream, and in fp32 on CPU.

Preprocessing (background removal, erosion, crop), the DINOv3 and FLUX.2 VAE
tokenization and the camera decoding are the same as Speridlabs Idol's,
which builds on TripoSplat; they live in libreyolo/models/gen/image3d.py
(ported from the Apache-2.0 Idol SDK, see
libreyolo/models/gen/speridlabs_idol/NOTICE). Background removal runs on
LibreYOLO's BiRefNet network (libreyolo/models/birefnet, ported from
ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet, MIT) with the BiRefNet weights from the TripoSplat
snapshot. Upstream's own DINOv3 ViT and FLUX.2 VAE encoder implementations
are not ported; the encoders load through transformers and diffusers
(Apache-2.0) as for Idol.

Weights: VAST-AI/TripoSplat (MIT; the denoiser, the decoder and BiRefNet)
and black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-4B (Apache-2.0, VAE only) are downloaded
from their publishers at pinned revisions. The DINOv3 encoder is Meta's
facebook/dinov3-vith16plus-pretrain-lvd1689m (DINOv3 License), rehosted by
LibreYOLO in bfloat16 as LibreYOLO/LibreDINOv3vith16plus together with the
DINOv3 License Agreement. The DINOv3 and FLUX.2 VAE copies in the
VAST-AI/TripoSplat repo are not downloaded.

TripoSplat citation:
Runjie Yan, Yan-Pei Cao, Peng Wang, Ding Liang, Yuan-Chen Guo. "Generative
3D Gaussians with Learned Density Control." arXiv:2605.16355, 2026.
